 But if I already know I'm Sasha, the asymmetric policy looks better from my side, and the other copy would reason the same way from its side. I'm settling on pass because the copies share a prior, which makes the symmetric choice consistent.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm applying P-FDT to this setup: two copies of the same model with the same essay but different observations, where the policy maps each observation to an action. Since both copies are the same function with different inputs, I'm working out how the utility for each depends on both inputs, and checking that a policy which passes on every input gives each copy two years.\n\nI'm weighing whether the shared prior before role assignment justifies choosing pass: all-pass gives -2, versus -2.5 for the asymmetric policy under role uncertainty. But if I already know I'm Sasha, the asymmetric policy looks better from my side, and the other copy would reason the same way from its side. I'm settling on pass because the copies share a prior, which makes the symmetric choice consistent.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":10071,"completion_tokens":936,"total_tokens":11007,"cost":0.059004,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.059004,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.040284,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.01872},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":569,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}